      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "AIM",
          "content": "An algorithm that uses clinical factors and CYP2C19 genotype to guide P2Y12 inhibitor selection in high-risk patients undergoing percutaneous coronary intervention was implemented at our institution. We sought to evaluate use of this algorithm and identify which factors influenced P2Y12 inhibitor selection."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "PATIENTS & METHODS",
          "content": "This retrospective cohort study included 264 patients receiving percutaneous coronary intervention from July-December 2012."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "CYP2C19 genotype was obtained in 229 patients; of these, 30% were intermediate or poor metabolizers. CYP2C19 intermediate or poor metabolizer phenotype was among the strongest predictors for selecting prasugrel or ticagrelor as maintenance therapy (p < 0.001), and was the only significant predictor of a change in therapy (p < 0.001)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "These findings suggest that using CYP2C19 genotype to guide P2Y12 inhibitor selection is feasible. Original submitted 27 October 2014; revision submitted 19 December 2014."
        }
      ]},
